Offline sync

The `Phone app` writes to a `Local database`, with the label `write`. When
online, the `Sync engine` reads the `Local database` with the label `read`, and
sends changes to the `Sync API` with the label `push`. The `Sync API` saves
them in the `Cloud database`, with the label `save`.
---
Phone app -> Local database: write
Sync engine -> Local database: read
Sync engine -> Sync API: push
Sync API -> Cloud database: save
